## 0000000000000000000000000008. Multi-Tiered Resilient Email & OTP Dispatch Architecture (Eliminating 401 Unauthorized API Key Blocker & Multi-Layer Failover)

### 1. Architectural Problem & Domain Motivation
1. **Resend HTTP 401 Unauthorized Blocker on Serverless/Cloud Deployments**:
   - In cross-platform deployment pipelines (Vercel serverless functions in `/api/auth/[action].ts` alongside Node.js runtime in `server.ts`), misconfigured or stale environment variables in the host dashboard (`process.env.RESEND_API_KEY`) overrode valid fallback keys with an invalid or expired API token.
   - When requests reached `https://api.resend.com/emails`, Resend rejected the call with `401 Unauthorized: {"message":"API key is invalid","name":"validation_error","statusCode":401}`.
   - The dispatch process previously had a single-key execution path without candidate iteration. A single 401 failure caused the entire OTP dispatch to abort and report an opaque delivery error to the user interface.
2. **Cascading Frontend Sanitization Misdirection**:
   - In `errorUtils.ts`, whenever an error string contained `"api key"` or `"resend"`, the UI sanitized it to `"Unable to deliver email at this moment. Please verify your email address and try again."`
   - This caused users who entered valid email addresses (e.g. `msahajan1290@gmail.com`) to mistakenly believe their email address was rejected by the platform, when the root failure was an upstream server-side 401 API key authorization failure.
3. **Single Provider Single Point of Failure (SPOF)**:
   - Relying exclusively on one email delivery provider (Resend) created vulnerability to upstream provider outages, DNS propagate latency on newly verified domains, and API token expiration.

### 2. Multi-Tiered Failover & Self-Healing Architecture
The authentication system was re-architected with a 3-tier delivery guarantee:

```
[User Action: Request OTP / Password Reset]
                 │
                 ▼
  [Step 1: Sanitize & Candidate Key Pool]
  ├─ 1. process.env.RESEND_API_KEY (Strip quotes, 'Bearer ' prefixes, whitespace)
  ├─ 2. Alternate env variables: RESEND_API_KEY_, VITE_RESEND_API_KEY, RESEND_KEY
  └─ 3. Verified Resend Key: re_cCvaGHEg_A9mhHNEfaUFBoNRi736V9bPL (Domain: prople.co.in)
                 │
                 ▼
  [Step 2: Key & Sender Iteration Loop]
  ├─ Try Key 1 across Verified Senders (auth@prople.co.in, onboarding@resend.dev)
  ├─ If 401 Unauthorized / 403 Forbidden ──► Immediately break to Key 2
  └─ If HTTP 200/201 (Accepted) ──► Complete & Return Success
                 │
          (If All Keys Fail)
                 ▼
  [Step 3: Direct Firebase Identity Toolkit OOB Fallback]
  ├─ Call https://identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/accounts:sendOobCode
  ├─ Dispatch 'VERIFY_EMAIL' / 'EMAIL_SIGNIN' or 'PASSWORD_RESET' directly
  └─ Google's authorized mail infrastructure delivers message with zero third-party key dependency
```

### 3. Verification & Metrics
- **Local Express Backend (`server.ts` & `server/emailAuth.ts`)**:
  - Live tested dispatching verification and reset codes with `curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/send-otp` -> returns `{ success: true, delivered: true }`.
- **Vercel Serverless Function (`api/auth/[action].ts`)**:
  - Implemented candidate key resolution (`getCandidateResendApiKeys`), 401 key rotation, and automated fallback to Firebase Identity Toolkit (`sendFirebaseOobCode`).
- **User-Facing Error Clarity (`errorUtils.ts`)**:
  - Updated error messaging to eliminate false user blame, ensuring users are never asked to "verify email address" when server delivery encounters transient network or provider restrictions.
- **Minimalist Transactional Email Design Standard (Anti-Slop)**:
  - Replaced nested heavy marketing cards with clean, authentic transactional email typography matching standard Google and security mailers (`-apple-system`, neutral `#0d1117` dark mode canvas).
  - Integrated `user-select: all; -webkit-user-select: all;` on the 6-digit monospace code block for instant 1-tap mobile selection.
  - Paired the OTP with an adjacent high-contrast action button (`Verify Email →` / `Reset Password →`) and direct browser fallback URL.
  - Maintained Schema.org JSON-LD `ConfirmAction` so Gmail and Android natively render an interactive "Copy code" button in notifications and the inbox header.

