## 00000000. Route-Based Crawlable App-Store Architecture & SSR SEO Blueprint
### 1. Architectural Transformation (SPA to Hybrid Server-Rendered Multi-Route Marketplace)
Prople Store transitions from a purely client-state-dependent Single Page Application (SPA) into a hybrid server-rendered, route-based web application with full search engine crawlability, static document indexing, and instant client-side hydration:
- **Canonical URL Hierarchy**:
  - `/`: Store landing and general marketplace homepage.
  - `/apps`: Global cross-platform application catalog.
  - `/apps/android`: Dedicated Android catalog and APK distribution hub.
  - `/apps/windows`: Windows binaries, executables, and desktop applications.
  - `/apps/linux`: Debian (.deb), AppImage, RPM, and Linux native packages.
  - `/apps/mac`: macOS (.dmg, .pkg) packages.
  - `/app/[slug]`: Canonical individual application page with unique title, description, SoftwareApplication Schema.org JSON-LD, BreadcrumbList JSON-LD, and pre-rendered semantic HTML.
  - `/category/[slug]`: Specific application category hub with ItemList structured data.
  - `/developer/[slug]`: Verified developer and organization profile page.
  - `/search?q=[query]`: Deep-linkable and shareable search results page.
- **Initial Document Pre-Rendering (No Empty Shells)**:
  - When an individual application URL (`/app/[slug]`) is requested directly by Googlebot, social crawlers (Twitterbot, WhatsApp, Discord, Slack), or users, the Express server injects complete application markup directly into `<div id="root">`.
  - The initial HTML contains the app's title, verified publisher, version, platform, rating, review breakdown, downloads, safety badges, full description, screenshot galleries, and direct binary download URLs.
  - When client-side JavaScript loads, React seamlessly takes over and mounts interactive controls (ratings, reviews, install progress animations, screenshots lightbox) without layout shifts or content re-fetching.
- **Zero-Duplicate Canonical Policy**:
  - URLs using legacy query parameters (e.g. `/?app=xyz`, `/app?id=xyz`, `/app/xyz?id=xyz`) are permanently redirected (HTTP 301/308) to the canonical `/app/[slug]`.
  - Avoids duplicate indexing penalties across Google Search, Bing, and AI crawlers.
- **Strict 404 HTTP Status Compliance**:
  - Requests for nonexistent applications (`/app/non-existent-app`) return true HTTP 404 responses with a themed Prople Store 404 error page, preventing soft 404 errors or false indexing.
- **Crawlable Semantic Links (`<a href="/app/[slug]">`)**:
  - All application cards across squircle rows, landscape banners, spotlight heroes, editorial features, top charts, and search results render genuine HTML anchors.
  - Users clicking with left mouse get smooth client-side state transitions via history pushState without full page reloads, while crawlers and middle/cmd-clicks follow genuine URLs.
- **Dynamic XML Sitemap & Robots.txt Directives**:
  - `/sitemap.xml` automatically aggregates all published applications, developer profiles, categories, platform portals, and policy pages with accurate `<lastmod>` timestamps.
