## 00. Social Link Preview & WhatsApp Unfurling Architecture (Dual-Logo System)

### The Dual-Logo Specification for Shared Applications
When an application link (e.g. `https://prople-store.domain/?app={appId}`) is shared in WhatsApp, Telegram, iMessage, Discord, or Facebook:
1. **Primary Side Image (The Bigger Visual)**: Must **always** be the authentic **Shared Application's Logo** (`app.iconUrl`), not the general store platform logo. This visually communicates which exact software package is being shared.
2. **Bottom Domain Badge (The Small Visual)**: Modern messaging clients (notably WhatsApp) parse `<link rel="icon" ...>` and `<link rel="shortcut icon" ...>` to render a tiny website badge beside the domain line (e.g. `🔗 prople... [Logo]`). This is where the Prople Store logo belongs.

### Technical Implementation Pillars
1. **Pure Link & Text Native Share Sheet (`shareUtils.ts`)**:
   - `shareAppNative` intentionally avoids attaching file/media blobs (`files: []`) in `navigator.share()`. Passing file blobs causes messaging platforms (especially WhatsApp and Telegram) to treat the share as a picture/media attachment rather than generating a clean, interactive URL card.
   - By dispatching exclusively `{ title, text, url }`, messaging clients receive the canonical link, trigger automated unfurling, and render the rich preview card.
2. **Server-Side Crawler Pre-Rendering (`server/seoRenderer.ts`)**:
   - `og:image` and `og:image:secure_url` are strictly resolved to the absolute HTTPS URL of the application's icon, accompanied by explicit `og:image:width: 300` and `og:image:height: 300` tags for compact card rendering.
   - `twitter:card` is set to `"summary"` to maintain the compact square side-thumbnail card layout in messaging apps.
   - High-resolution store icons (`/logo.png`) are served via `<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="192x192">` so scrapers extract the store logo exclusively for the bottom domain attribution badge.
3. **In-Memory Sub-10ms Crawler Cache (`server.ts`)**:
   - `seoAppsCache` caches queried application document metadata in memory for 10 minutes, ensuring external bot crawlers (User-Agent `WhatsApp/2.x`, `facebookexternalhit`, `Twitterbot`, etc.) receive instant 200 responses with hydrated meta tags before socket timeout thresholds.

