## 1. "New" Tag & Release Qualification Algorithm

### Current Mechanism
The store currently assigns the green "New" badge to an app when:
- An app is newly published and has not yet reached a statistically reliable review threshold (e.g. `rating === 0 || rating == null`).
- In this state, the numeric star rating (e.g., `0.0 ★`) is suppressed in favor of the clean **"New"** badge to avoid user churn or unfair low perception.

### Mathematical Production Formula
To ensure high quality, fair distribution, and automated graduation:

$$\text{IsNew} = (\text{now} - \text{createdAt} \le 30\text{ days}) \lor (\text{ratingCount} < 5)$$

- **Graduation Condition**: Once an application exceeds 30 days since publishing AND has accumulated $\ge 5$ verified community reviews, it automatically graduates from the "New" badge to display its Bayesian-weighted community rating score.
- **Update Frequency**: Calculated dynamically on feed generation and memoized in Firestore/Redis per app entity.

