## 5. Store Ranking & Recommendation Algorithms

### A. Bayesian Rating Average
Avoids bias where an app with 1 five-star review ranks higher than an app with 500 reviews averaging 4.8 stars:

$$S = \frac{v \cdot R + m \cdot C}{v + m}$$

Where:
- $v$ = number of reviews for the app
- $R$ = average rating of the app
- $m$ = minimum threshold of reviews required (e.g., $m = 10$)
- $C$ = mean rating across the entire store catalog (e.g., $C = 4.2$)

### B. Trending & Velocity Score
Determines "Trending" feed placement based on short-term momentum rather than cumulative all-time volume:

$$\text{Velocity} = \frac{D_{\text{last 7 days}} \times 2.0 + V_{\text{last 7 days}} \times 0.5 + R_{\text{last 7 days}} \times 3.0}{(T + 2)^{1.2}}$$

Where:
- $D$ = verified installs
- $V$ = unique page views
- $R$ = positive ratings / reviews
- $T$ = time elapsed in days since the launch / update

### C. Category & Similarity Clustering
- TF-IDF or cosine similarity across title, tags, description, and permission signatures to cluster similar applications and power the "Similar Apps" recommendation carousel.

