## 10. Search Engine (Google/Bing) & AI Engine (GEO) Positioning Blueprint

### A. Root-Cause Analysis: Why Prior Search Results Showed Outdated Trademarked Phrasing
When Google, Perplexity, or Gemini AI Overviews crawled `https://www.prople.co.in`, they parsed the exact `<meta name="description">` tag and `<script type="application/ld+json">` snippet in `index.html`. 

Previously, an old legacy HTML snippet had copied descriptive text mentioning third-party app store naming.

Because web bots prioritize author-declared metadata:
1. The AI engine extracted that outdated phrase as the platform's primary feature.
2. The search result completely omitted the store's primary value propositions: **Cross-platform downloads (Android APK, Windows, Linux, and Web PWAs)**, safe one-click installation, ratings & reviews, and independent developer publishing.

### B. Trademark & Brand Protection Directive
- **Strict Prohibition**: Never use third-party trademarked names in HTML meta tags, Schema.org entities, UI labels, code comments, or website descriptions.
- **Risks**: Trademark dilution, automated infringement notices, search engine de-indexing, and legal brand exposure.
- **Standard**: Describe functionality strictly using domain-generic terminology (e.g., "independent application marketplace", "cross-platform app store", "production-grade high-resolution asset management", "developer release console").

### C. Full Feature Value Positioning for Search Engines & AI Crawlers
Search engine snippets and AI Overviews must clearly articulate the 5 flagship capabilities:
1. **Cross-Platform App Downloads**: Native support for downloading and installing apps across Android (APK), Windows (.exe, .msi), Linux (.deb, .AppImage), and Web (PWA).
2. **Direct Verified Installs**: Safe, verified application packages with SHA verification and real-time installation tracking.
3. **Live Web Previews**: Instant in-browser interactive testing before downloading.
4. **Community Trust Signals**: Transparent ratings, verified developer replies, and structured Data Safety disclosures.
5. **Independent Developer Console**: Multi-platform release management, GitHub Release sync, and asset optimization.

### D. Upgraded SEO & Schema.org Implementation
- **`<title>`**: `Prople Store – Android Apps & Games Marketplace`
- **`<meta name="description">`**: `Discover Android apps and games on Prople Store, an app marketplace operated by Cloaktail Industries. Verified APK downloads, ratings, and developer publishing.`
- **Schema.org Structured Data**:
  - `@type`: `WebApplication`
  - `applicationCategory`: `ApplicationMarketplace`
  - `operatingSystem`: `Android, Windows, Linux, Web`
  - `featureList`: Includes verified Android APK downloads, safe installers, live web app sandbox, and developer console.
- **Server Pre-Rendering**: `server/seoRenderer.ts` dynamically serves canonical `<title>`, `<meta>`, Schema.org, and crawlable `<noscript>` text for deep-linked app landing pages (`/app/:id`), guaranteeing that every individual app package is indexed directly in Google search with direct "Install" intent.

