## 16. Platform Moderation Consequences, Enforcement Mechanics & State Machine

### Objective & Architectural Blueprint
When an administrator performs moderation actions (blocking an app, suspending a publisher, restricting a publisher, or making apps private), the platform enforces immediate real-time results rather than passive badge updates.

### Complete Moderation Actions & Real-world Consequences

| Admin Action | Scope | Direct Store & User Consequences | Technical Enforcement Point |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Ban / Block App** | Single App | 1. App is **immediately hidden** from all public discovery (`allAppListings`), including Home, Categories, Top Charts, and Search.<br>2. Direct deep links (`/app/:id`) show an official suspended advisory banner.<br>3. Install / Download APK actions are **completely disabled**.<br>4. App is flagged in Publisher Console with a red suspended status.<br>5. Direct notification dispatched to the publisher's phone. | `StoreConfigContext` filter (`allAppListings`), `AboutAppPage.tsx`, `AdminModerationService.isAppBlockedOrSuspended()` |
| **Set App Private** | Single App | 1. App is removed from public store browsing and search (`allAppListings`).<br>2. Only the publisher (in Publisher Console) and Platform Administrators can access the listing.<br>3. Does not penalize the publisher's account reputation. | `StoreConfigContext` filtering on `isPrivate` |
| **Suspend / Block Publisher** | Publisher (All Apps) | 1. **All applications** by that publisher are instantly removed from the public store catalogue.<br>2. Publisher is blocked from submitting new apps or updates in Developer Console.<br>3. Direct security notification dispatched to publisher's device. | `StoreConfigContext` checks `isPublisherBlocked(app.developer)`, `PublisherConsolePage` blocks uploads |
| **Restrict Publisher** | Publisher Account | 1. Publisher account is placed on probationary standing.<br>2. Submission quotas are throttled and newly submitted updates are flagged for mandatory manual admin approval.<br>3. Warning notification sent to publisher's device. | `AdminModerationService.isPublisherRestricted()`, Developer Console submission pipeline |
| **Take All Apps Private** | Publisher Batch | 1. Instantly flips `isPrivate: true` across all applications published under that publisher name.<br>2. Removes all entries from public store discovery while preserving listings for future reactivation. | `AdminControlPanel.tsx` batch execution + `refreshCatalogue()` |
| **Make All Apps Public** | Publisher Batch | 1. Restores `isPrivate: false` across all applications published by that publisher.<br>2. Immediately re-indexes and surfaces them in public store feeds. | `AdminControlPanel.tsx` batch execution + `refreshCatalogue()` |
| **Permanently Ban Release Link / Repo** | Link / Repository | 1. Blacklists GitHub profile, repository, or direct APK download URL.<br>2. Any app referencing this source URL is prevented from publishing or downloading. | `AdminModerationService.isReleaseLinkBanned()`, download & publish resolvers |
| **Broadcast Global Notice** | All Users | 1. Immediately injects notification into Firestore global feed (`store_notifications`).<br>2. Triggers active phone notifications on all connected devices.<br>3. Appears in Notification Centre with category styling and deep links. | `firestoreNotificationService.sendGlobalBroadcastNotice()`, live snapshot listeners |

### Event-Driven Invalidation & Real-Time Sync
To prevent stale states where badges change but catalogue listings persist:
1. **Firestore Real-Time Snapshots**: `AdminModerationService` maintains active `onSnapshot` subscriptions to `app_moderation`, `publisher_restrictions`, and `banned_releases`.
2. **Cross-Window Custom Event (`admin:moderation:updated`)**: Whenever a moderation change arrives, an internal window event is dispatched.
3. **Store Catalogue Invalidation (`moderationVersion`)**: `StoreConfigContext` listens to `admin:moderation:updated` and increments `moderationVersion`, automatically re-evaluating `allAppListings` and purging blocked/suspended apps from the live store without requiring a manual page reload.

