## 28. Google Play Store Dynamic Ambient Colored Shadow & Inward Side Border Glow Architecture

### Problem Statement & Visual Objective
In the native Google Play Store web and mobile client:
1. **Uncovered Upper Banner Artwork**: The top ~75% and upper side borders of the banner image remain completely crisp, bright, and unobstructed without artificial border covers or heavy full-perimeter inner glows.
2. **Strong Ambient Title Background at the Bottom of the Image**: At the bottom of the banner graphic where the headline/event title is written, the background behind the title is enveloped in a strong, rich ambient color wash dynamically extracted from the banner graphic's bottom and dominant tones.
3. **Multi-Stop Ambient Diffusion & Frosted Backdrop**: Instead of a plain black scrim or muddy darkening, this title background blends a high-opacity vertical gradient ($0.95 \to 0.42 \to \text{transparent}$) with horizontal side color bleeding and hardware-accelerated `backdrop-filter: blur(16px)`, producing the signature Google Play glowing ambient title stage with razor-sharp typography.

### Architecture & Implementation Blueprint
To achieve 60fps rendering without UI layout shifts or performance regressions:

1. **In-Memory Caching & Bottom Area Color Extraction (`bannerAmbientService.ts`)**:
   - **Canvas Analysis**: Renders the banner image down to an asynchronous 32x20 offscreen canvas with `crossOrigin = 'anonymous'`.
   - **Localized Bottom Sampling**: Samples the lower rows ($y \in [12, 19]$) specifically representing the title zone, along with lower-left, lower-right, and central dominant clusters.
   - **Enrichment Engine (`enrichTone`)**: Elevates dark or low-chroma bottom regions into luminous jewel-like tones so the ambient background always emits authentic vibrant color.
   - **LRU / Map Memoization**: Extracted ambient styles are cached in an in-memory `Map<string, BannerAmbientColors>`, ensuring zero redundant canvas computations across carousel navigation.

2. **Harmonious Natural Sampled Color Pipeline (Fixed Borderless Layout)**:
   - **Artwork-Derived Normal Color Extraction (`buildNaturalBannerAmbient`)**:
     - Extracts the natural primary hue directly from the bottom region and dominant cluster of the banner graphic (no artificial opposing/complementary hue shift).
     - Derives `deepBase` ($L \approx 11\%$, $S \approx 50-80\%$) matching the image's own palette, guaranteeing WCAG AAA text legibility (> 14:1) that never washes out under bright artwork while remaining 100% harmonious with the original art.
     - Derives `vibrantMid` ($L \approx 42\%$) along with natural corner blooms (`leftTone` and `rightTone`) sampled directly from the image edges.
   - **Fixed Borderless Radial Dispersion (Zero Straight Lines, Zero Blur)**:
     ```ts
     background: [
       `radial-gradient(ellipse 135% 82% at 50% 100%, rgba(${dbr}, ${dbg}, ${dbb}, 0.95) 0%, rgba(${dbr}, ${dbg}, ${dbb}, 0.85) 45%, rgba(${vmr}, ${vmg}, ${vmb}, 0.35) 75%, transparent 100%)`,
       `radial-gradient(ellipse 75% 65% at 0% 100%, rgba(${lr}, ${lg}, ${lb}, 0.65) 0%, transparent 70%)`,
       `radial-gradient(ellipse 75% 65% at 100% 100%, rgba(${rr}, ${rg}, ${rb}, 0.65) 0%, transparent 70%)`,
     ].join(', ')
     ```
   - **Clean Typography & Dot-Free Badges**:
     - Ultra-bold display headline (`font-extrabold text-[14.5px] sm:text-[16px] leading-[1.3] text-white`) with high-depth drop shadows (`drop-shadow-[0_2px_4px_rgba(0,0,0,0.95)]`).
     - Pure, clean uppercase eyebrow tag without artificial color dots.
     - Minimalist frosted glass event badge without artificial color dots.
   - **Native App Details Separation**: The app details section below remains clean, crisp, and high-contrast on native Google Play dark surfaces (`dark:bg-[#1e1f23]`).

3. **Exact 16:9 Banner Architecture (Upload & In-Use Standardization)**:
   - **Upload Validation & Ingestion (`inspectImage` / `AppMediaUploader`)**:
     - Standardized on strict 16:9 widescreen proportions ($16/9 \approx 1.7778$).
     - Replaced legacy $1024 \times 500$ ($2.048:1$) banner requirements with exact 16:9 validation (`Math.abs(aspectRatio - 16/9) < 0.035` and $width \ge 640$).
     - High-definition auto-fitting via canvas (`fitImageToCanvas(featureGraphicUrl, 1920, 1080, 'cover')`) and compression targeting full 1080p resolution ($1920 \times 1080$).
   - **In-Use Presentation (`HeroSpotlightCard` & `EditorialFeatureCard`)**:
     - Banner image frames strictly enforce `aspect-[16/9]` on all viewports, eliminating subtle aspect ratio drift across screen sizes.
     - Preserves the exact existing card layout, rounded geometry (`rounded-[24px] sm:rounded-[26px]`), connected bottom app card, and carousel margins without any disruption.

4. **Secondary Banner Tag & Border Removal History**:
   - Stripped legacy floating pill badges that had boxy borders (`border border-white/20`) over banner artwork.

5. **Spotlight Badge Tag Restoration & Borderless Architecture**:
   - Restored the Spotlight Badge Tag on 16:9 banner spotlight cards (`HeroSpotlightCard`, `EditorialFeatureCard`, and `AppDetailPage`) derived from Publisher Console `spotlightBadge` metadata, with fallback to app category or 'Featured'.
   - Enforced complete borderless pill geometry (`bg-white/95 text-neutral-900 font-semibold border-0 border-none shadow-sm rounded-full px-2.5 sm:px-3 py-1`) at `top-3 left-3 sm:top-3.5 sm:left-3.5`, providing clean, high-contrast, border-free tag chips on any banner artwork.

6. **Google Play App Details Stats & Package Verification Alignment**:
   - In `AppDetailPage`, replaced the 3rd stat column beside the app icon (previously package size) with community Downloads count (e.g. `10Cr+`, `1M+`, `Downloads`), matching Google Play's exact three-column metrics hierarchy:
     1. **Rating & Reviews**: Average numeric rating with star icon + formatted review count modal trigger.
     2. **Content Rating**: Age qualification badge + localized descriptor.
     3. **Downloads**: Scaled community installation volume (`app.downloads`).
   - Relocated unified app package size directly beside the verification subline below the primary install action button: e.g. `'Free • Verified Android APK • 45 MB'`.

7. **16:9 Banner & Transparent Scroll-Away Header (`AppDetailPage`)**:
