## 27. Light Mode Google Play Cloud Mist Architecture & Contrast System

### 1. Authentic Play Store Cloud Mist Banner Dissolve
- **Problem**: In light mode, banner ambient washes (`ambientColors.titleBackgroundStyle`) designed for dark backgrounds produce dark indigo/charcoal shadows (`rgba(12, 16, 28, ...)`). When combined with linear gradients to white and negative margins (`-mt-10 sm:-mt-14`), this created a muddy, dark oval behind the application title and developer name.
- **Atmospheric Clouding Engine**:
  - `ambientColors.titleBackgroundStyle` is strictly isolated to dark mode (`hidden dark:block`), leaving the banner art vibrant and pure in light mode.
  - An authentic, multi-stop cloud mist layer is introduced exclusively in light mode (`block dark:hidden`):
    - Multi-stop vertical dissolve: `linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255,255,255,0) 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0.08) 20%, rgba(255,255,255,0.32) 42%, rgba(255,255,255,0.68) 65%, rgba(255,255,255,0.92) 84%, #ffffff 100%)`.
    - Atmospheric radial plume: `radial-gradient(ellipse 135% 85% at 50% 100%, #ffffff 0%, rgba(255,255,255,0.96) 48%, rgba(255,255,255,0.55) 76%, transparent 100%)`.
  - Content positioning is decoupled: light mode utilizes `-mt-2 sm:-mt-4 md:-mt-5`, seating developer typography naturally on the pure white cloud transition, while dark mode maintains its native `-mt-10 sm:-mt-14 md:-mt-16` overlap with 0% changes.

### 2. Tailwind Variant Regularization & WCAG Contrast Guarantee
- **Tailwind Pseudo-Class Correction**: Resolved instances of invalid `light:` prefix syntax in `HeroSpotlightCard` and `EditorialFeatureCard`. In standard Tailwind CSS, unprefixed utility classes define the light mode baseline and `dark:` overrides define dark mode.
- **Hierarchy Regularization**:
  - App Titles: `text-neutral-900 dark:text-white` (replaces washed-out white text on light card backgrounds).
  - Developer & Sublines: `text-neutral-600 dark:text-[#9aa0a6]`.
  - Ratings & Badges: `text-neutral-900 dark:text-white` with amber star and bordered badge `border-neutral-400 dark:border-neutral-500/60`.
  - Action Buttons: `bg-[#0b57d0] hover:bg-[#0842a0] text-white` in light mode, preserving `dark:bg-[#a8c7fa] dark:hover:bg-[#8ab4f8] dark:text-[#003366]` in dark mode.
  - Zero Dark Mode Alterations: Dark mode styles remain 100% untouched and identical in both layout and color values.

