## 32. AI Studio GitHub Import Migration & Runtime Normalization

### 1. Architectural Mandate
When migrating repositories imported from external GitHub repositories (`sam-live2c/AppMarket`), the runtime environment requires strict compliance with Node.js 22 LTS web constraints:
- **Package Manager Consolidation**: Exclusive use of `npm` for dependency resolution and script executions. Elimination of auxiliary locks (`bun.lock`, `yarn.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`) to prevent non-deterministic lock collisions.
- **Port & Host Binding**: Dev and production servers must bind to `0.0.0.0:3000`. In `server.ts`, Express listens on `3000` with host `0.0.0.0`.
- **Search & Storage Resilience**: External indexing services (e.g. Meilisearch) must employ fail-fast health probes with bounded race timeouts (2500ms) and automatic fallback to in-memory/Firestore catalog scoring to guarantee continuous operational availability when Meilisearch is not provisioned.
- **Metadata Synchronization**: `metadata.json`, `<title>`, OpenGraph, Twitter Cards, and Schema.org JSON-LD maintain strict parity with parent organization branding (Prople Store / Cloaktail Industries).
- **Environment Parity**: All backend secrets and integration endpoints (Firebase, Gemini API, GitHub Tokens, Meilisearch) are explicitly specified in `.env.example`.

