## 48. Security Hardening, Vulnerability Mitigation & RFC 9116 Security Directives

### Context & Scanner Findings (Pentest-Tools Web Vulnerability Audit)
Following penetration testing and security scanning against `https://www.prople.co.in/`, the platform mitigated four core compliance findings:
1. **Missing Referrer-Policy Header (CWE-693, OWASP A02:2025 / A5:2021)**: Risk of leaking originating URLs, query parameters, or internal state when users navigate via outbound links.
2. **Missing Content-Security-Policy (CSP) Header (CWE-1021, OWASP A02:2025)**: Risk of XSS or unverified script execution in absence of strict origin controls.
3. **Missing X-Content-Type-Options Header (CWE-693)**: MIME-sniffing risks in browsers that could execute non-script assets as JavaScript.
4. **Missing `security.txt` File (RFC 9116, CWE-1188, SOC 2 CC7.4)**: Absence of a machine-readable security vulnerability disclosure channel.
5. **Technology & Server Fingerprinting (CWE-200)**: Default server banners and headers (e.g., `X-Powered-By: Express`).
6. **Crawler Email Harvesting (CWE-200)**: Plaintext email exposure in root HTML document crawls.

### Comprehensive Mitigation Architecture

#### 1. Server-Side & Edge CDN HTTP Security Headers
Configured synchronously across Express (`server.ts`) and Vercel Edge (`vercel.json`):
- `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`: Strips origin paths on cross-origin requests while retaining full URLs for same-origin navigation.
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`: Strictly instructs browsers to trust declared MIME types and never perform MIME sniffing.
- `Content-Security-Policy`:
  - `default-src 'self'`
  - `script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://apis.google.com https://*.firebaseio.com https://*.googleapis.com https://www.youtube.com https://s.ytimg.com`
  - `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com`
  - `font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com`
  - `img-src 'self' data: blob: https: http:`
  - `media-src 'self' blob: https:`
  - `connect-src 'self' https: wss: http: ws:`
  - `frame-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com https://*.firebaseapp.com https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com`
  - `frame-ancestors 'self' https:` (Mitigates clickjacking while enabling secure preview embeds).
  - `object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'`
- `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`
- `X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block`
- `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload`
- `Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()`

#### 2. RFC 9116 Standard `security.txt`
Served at both `/.well-known/security.txt` and `/security.txt` with MIME type `text/plain; charset=utf-8`:
- Declares official vulnerability intake endpoints: `mailto:cloaktailsupport@gmail.com` and `mailto:cloaktailofficial@gmail.com`.
- Declares canonical URL, expiration timestamp (`Expires: 2027-12-31T23:59:59.000Z`), language preferences (`Preferred-Languages: en`), and security policy links.
- Backed by static files in `public/` and dynamic Express fallback routes in `server.ts`.

#### 3. Technology Fingerprint & Email Exposure Elimination
- `app.disable('x-powered-by')` added to suppress server engine identification.
- `res.removeHeader('Server')` and `res.removeHeader('X-Powered-By')` enforced on all responses.
- Root HTML (`index.html`) Schema.org metadata sanitized: raw email strings replaced with structured `ContactPoint` pointing to `/.well-known/security.txt`, blocking automated scrapers while providing authorized researchers direct intake documentation.

