## 50. Strict Content-Security-Policy (CSP) Hardening & Zero-Inline Execution

### Audit Findings Remediation (Pentest-Tools Verified)
Pentest-Tools light & deep security scan identified three specific vectors in the initial CSP:
1. `frame-ancestors`: Inclusion of `https:` wildcard allowed third-party framing.
2. `script-src`: Presence of `'unsafe-eval'` allowed DOM code execution via `eval()`.
3. `script-src`: Presence of `'unsafe-inline'` allowed unhashed in-page script execution.

### Architectural Solution & Engineering Remediation
1. **Confinement of `frame-ancestors` to `'self'`**:
   - In production (`vercel.json`), `frame-ancestors` is strictly locked to `'self'`, mitigating CWE-1021 and OWASP Top 10 A02:2025 (Security Misconfiguration / Clickjacking) while aligning with `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`.
   - In development server (`server.ts`), environment detection (`isDev`) securely permits developer studio iframe previews (`https://*.run.app https://*.google.com`) while enforcing `'self'` in production.

2. **Elimination of `'unsafe-eval'`**:
   - Removed `'unsafe-eval'` completely from both Edge configuration (`vercel.json`) and application server (`server.ts`). Verified that neither Vite runtime, Firebase SDK, nor React modules invoke `eval()`.

3. **Zero-Inline Script Execution (`'unsafe-inline'` Elimination)**:
   - Extracted pre-hydration theme initialization script from `index.html` directly into `src/main.tsx` module scope.
   - Removed duplicate manual service worker registration script from `index.html`; SW lifecycle is safely driven by `vite-plugin-pwa` generated `/registerSW.js` and `main.tsx`.
   - Removed `'unsafe-inline'` from `script-src` in `vercel.json` and production `server.ts`.
   - Only trusted origin scripts (`'self'`) and necessary external Google / Firebase / YouTube APIs are whitelisted.

