## 33. Isolated Logo Architecture & Multi-Scale Transparent Asset Pipeline

### 1. Problem Statement & Design Intent
Historically, PWA icons, favicons, and vector SVGs were packaged inside a solid dark rectangle (`#131314` container box). This introduced artificial boxed borders on light themes, in browser tabs, and within OS app launchers. The objective was to liberate the brand mark into an **isolated emblem** with transparent alpha channels across all display contexts.

### 2. Algorithmic Asset Extraction & Alpha Un-Multiplication
1. **Background Masking**: The background canvas (`#131314` / R=19, G=19, B=20) was dynamically masked to zero opacity (`a = 0`).
2. **Anti-Aliased Edge Un-Blending**: Boundary transition pixels were un-multiplied against the `#131314` background tone using:
   $$C_{\text{unblended}} = \frac{C_{\text{composite}} - C_{\text{bg}} \cdot (1 - \alpha)}{\alpha}$$
   This completely eliminates dark halos and dark-fringe artifacts when rendered on light or translucent surfaces.
3. **Area-Averaged Resampling with Premultiplied Alpha**:
   Downsampling from 512x512 to 192x192, 180x180, 48x48, 32x32, and 16x16 utilized premultiplied alpha area-coverage accumulation, ensuring optimal sharpness, crisp geometric edges, and zero gamma distortion.
4. **Multi-Format Asset Coverage**:
   - `public/icon.svg`: Pure vector container embedding the transparent isolated PNG without `<rect>` background.
   - `public/favicon.ico`: Multi-resolution container (16x16, 32x32, 48x48) with full alpha channel.
   - `public/favicon.png`: 32x32 transparent PNG.
   - `public/pwa-192x192.png`: 192x192 transparent PWA launcher icon.
   - `public/pwa-512x512.png`: 512x512 high-resolution transparent PWA launcher icon.
   - `public/apple-touch-icon.png`: 180x180 transparent Apple touch icon.
   - `public/logo.png` & `src/assets/images/logo.png`: 512x512 transparent brand assets.
   - `src/components/BrandLogo.tsx`: Updated to render the isolated emblem seamlessly without artificial square container borders.

