## 43. Mobile-Native Edge-to-Edge Viewport Integration & Zero-CLS Sizing Blueprint

### 1. The Core Architecture: Full-Bleed Carousel & Edge Alignment
In modern native mobile app stores (e.g. Google Play Store), the entire mobile screen is utilized without artificial parent padding or boxed gutters that restrict swiping gestures:
- **Parent Feed Container**: Uses full-width flow (`py-3 flex flex-col gap-6 w-full overflow-x-hidden`) without an outer `px-4` box that clips carousels early.
- **Section Headers & Static Sections**: Padded with standard `px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-8` to maintain crisp typography alignment with the top app bar and subtabs.
- **Carousel Scroll Containers**: Utilize full-bleed horizontal scroll containers (`w-full overflow-x-auto scrollbar-hide px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-8`) with `overscroll-x-contain` and hardware touch acceleration (`touch-action: pan-x pan-y`).
- **First-Item Alignment**: The `px-4` on the carousel scroll view aligns the first card precisely with the section header and top bar.
- **Swipe Physics**: When swiped, cards slide all the way across the display without getting cropped 16px early inside an artificial parent box.

### 2. Universal Mobile Width Calculations (320px–430px Devices)
To ensure the subsequent card peeks with a consistent, intentional affordance across all device form factors:
- **Hero Spotlight & Editorial Cards**:
  $$\text{CardWidth} = \text{calc}(100\text{vw} - 48\text{px})$$
  With container padding of $16\text{px}$ and gap of $16\text{px}$, the subsequent card peeks exactly by $16\text{px}$ on every screen from $320\text{px}$ (iPhone SE / compact Android) to $430\text{px}$ (iPhone Pro Max / Pixel XL).
- **Landscape Video & Column Stack Cards**:
  $$\text{CardWidth} = \text{calc}(100\text{vw} - 56\text{px})$$
  Provides a clean $26\text{px}$ peek affordance for 16:9 widescreen previews and 3-row stacked columns.
- **Squircle App Icon Rows**:
  $$\text{CardWidth} = 92\text{px}\ (\text{mobile}),\ 100\text{px}\ (\text{tablet}),\ 104\text{px}\ (\text{desktop})$$
  Fits 3 full squircle icons on mobile with the 4th icon peeking gracefully.

### 3. Zero Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) Skeleton Synchronization
To eliminate any visual jump or settling after data loads:
