## 45. Developer Console Platform Sustainability & Milestone Donation Algorithm

### Objective
Provide non-intrusive, milestone-based sponsorship and sustainability prompts for active publishers on the Prople Developer Console. Rather than nagging publishers repeatedly or displaying persistent ads, the system celebrates meaningful publishing milestones and invites voluntary contributions to keep the store free, zero-commission, and fast.

### Milestone Progression Formula
The reminder modal is triggered exclusively at defined publishing milestones:
- **First Milestone**: When reaching **2 published apps** (celebrating initial creator adoption).
- **Subsequent Milestones**: At **10 apps, 20 apps, 30 apps, 40 apps, 50 apps...** (every multiple of 10 thereafter).

$$\text{CurrentMilestone}(n) = \begin{cases} 
2 & \text{if } 2 \le n < 10 \\ 
\lfloor \frac{n}{10} \rfloor \times 10 & \text{if } n \ge 10 \\ 
0 & \text{if } n < 2 
\end{cases}$$

### Anti-Spam & State Persistence Rules
1. **Acknowledged Milestones Array**:
   - Stored in `localStorage` under `prople_developer_donation_milestones` as a distinct set of numbers (e.g. `[2, 10, 20]`).
   - Backward compatible with legacy `prople_developer_donation_popup_shown` flag.
2. **Monotonic Progression Guarantee**:
   - A milestone $M$ is only triggered if $M \notin \text{ShownMilestones}$ and $M > 0$.
   - When a milestone $M$ is shown, all subordinate tiers ($\le M$) are automatically backfilled as satisfied.
   - Deleting and re-publishing apps (e.g. fluctuating between 9 and 10 apps) will **never** re-trigger an already acknowledged milestone.
3. **Contextual Congratulatory Copy**:
   - The modal dynamically adapts its header and note to celebrate the specific milestone achieved (e.g., "Congratulations on publishing your first 2 apps!" vs "Milestone reached: Congratulations on publishing 20 apps!").

