Generic call-to-action buttons such as "Download for Windows", "Download Linux Package", or vague "Download" labels obscure the actual binary distribution format. Users need to know upfront whether an app distributes as a standalone executable, container image, or native package installer prior to initiating transfers.

### Algorithmic Format Resolution (`getAppFormatExtension` & `getAppActionFileLabel`)
1. **Multi-Source Format Detection**:
   - Inspects publisher manifest `packageFormat`.
   - Fallback to asset URI and download URL extension parsing (`.dmg`, `.pkg`, `.exe`, `.msi`, `.msix`, `.appimage`, `.deb`, `.rpm`, `.tar.gz`, `.apk`, `.aab`).
