## 82. Cross-Browser Mobile Viewport, Stacking Context & Bottom Navigation Suppression Architecture

### Problem & Cross-Browser Discrepancy
1. **Root-Level Bottom Navigation Bleed-Over**:
   `MarketplaceShell` (`Layout.tsx`) persistently rendered the mobile bottom navigation bar (`<BottomNav>`) at `fixed bottom-0 z-40` on mobile viewports whenever `activeTab === 'you'`, without checking whether the active sub-view (`youView`) was an inner dedicated full-screen page such as `'studio'` (AppConsole / Publishing Form), `'admin-panel'`, `'edit-profile'`, etc.
2. **WebKit & Mobile Stacking Context Occlusion**:
   On iOS Safari and certain mobile browsers, `<main>` and its tab containers create an isolated stacking context. When `AppConsole` rendered its publishing bottom action bar (`Cancel`, `Back`, `Publish App`), the root `<BottomNav>` (`Games | Apps | Search | You`) was positioned directly on top of the bottom buttons, completely obscuring them and intercepting touch events.
3. **Double Header Rendering**:
   Similarly, the Marketplace header ("Prople Store" with search and notifications) was rendered above the sub-view, pushing down the page's dedicated header and causing layout anomalies across different device viewports.

### Architectural Resolution
1. **Sub-View Detection & Bottom Navigation Suppression (`Layout.tsx`)**:
   Introduced `isSubViewInYou = activeTab === 'you' && Boolean(youView && youView !== 'main')`. When active, `shouldHideHeader` and `shouldHideBottomNav` dynamically suppress the store header and bottom navigation bar, ensuring 100% of vertical screen space is granted to the dedicated full-screen view.
2. **Container Height & Overflow Normalization (`App.tsx`)**:
   Updated the tab scroll container (`data-tab-scroll="you"`) to switch from `overflow-y-auto` and `pb-[calc(68px+env(safe-area-inset-bottom,12px))]` to `h-full overflow-hidden` and clean `h-full flex flex-col` when in sub-views. This eliminates phantom scroll rails and preventing parent padding from pushing action buttons off-screen.
3. **Elevated & Safe-Area Aware Bottom Action Bar (`AppConsole.tsx`)**:
   Anchored the publishing form's bottom navigation action bar with `relative z-30`, `border-t border-theme-border/40`, subtle elevation shadow `shadow-[0_-4px_16px_rgba(0,0,0,0.15)]`, and iOS safe-area inset `pb-[max(1rem,env(safe-area-inset-bottom,16px))]`. The buttons (`Back`, `Cancel`, `Next`, `Publish App`) are prominently visible and fully accessible across all mobile and desktop browsers.

