## 80. Direct 1-Click Real Package Download & In-Platform Release Architecture

### 1. On-Site Automatic Download Without GitHub Redirect
- **Problem**: When triggering downloads directly with external GitHub release URLs (`https://github.com/.../releases/download/...`), mobile browsers (such as Chrome on Android) treat cross-origin downloads as document navigations, opening new tabs and redirecting the user away from Prople Store onto GitHub.
- **Solution**: 
  - `dispatchInstantNativeDownload` routes package downloads via the same-origin streaming endpoint (`/api/download-apk?url=...&name=...`) and activates it through a hidden zero-size `<iframe>` element.
  - Because the request is same-origin and returns `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="app.apk"` with the exact binary MIME type, the user **stays on the store page**.
  - Chrome on Android immediately intercepts the attachment in the background and starts the native download notification in the notification bar (`Downloading app.apk`) with **zero redirect to GitHub**, **zero tab changes**, and **zero RAM memory accumulation**.

### 2. In-Platform Direct App Releasing
- **Problem**: Previously, App Console Step 1 strictly required a GitHub repository release URL, preventing developers who host their own APKs or binaries from releasing apps directly on the platform.
- **Solution**:
  - `AppConsole.tsx` now supports direct application releases! Users can enter a direct APK / binary download URL (`https://your-server.com/app.apk`, S3, Cloudflare, Google Drive, or any direct link) OR import from GitHub.
  - The release wizard extracts the package name, auto-detects the platform (Android APK, Windows EXE/MSI, Linux AppImage/DEB, macOS DMG), and guides the developer through Steps 1 to 6 to set app identity, graphics, descriptions, permissions, and publish.
  - Published apps appear immediately live in Prople Store search, categories, and catalogs.

