## 81. Dynamic Viewport Media Architecture & Anti-Mobile-Centric Desktop Optimization

### 1. Viewport Differentiation & The Stretched Banner Anti-Pattern
- **Problem Identified**:
  - On mobile portrait screens (360px-430px wide), displaying a full-width 16:9 banner across the top with ambient fade and floating action buttons provides a focused, native mobile experience.
  - When viewed in **Desktop Mode** (monitors, laptops, tablets, or mobile Chrome with "Desktop site" toggled), stretching the same mobile top banner to full desktop container width (`max-w-5xl aspect-[16/9]`) caused the banner to expand vertically to over 550px-600px tall.
  - This pushed the app icon, title, stats, download CTA, and screenshots below the fold, forcing desktop users to scroll through a giant stretched image just to see basic app information.

### 2. The Dynamic Viewport Solution (Side-by-Side Marketplace Hero)
- **Mobile Viewport (`< md`)**:
  - Maintains the compact, vertical mobile layout: top 16:9 banner with immersive bottom atmospheric gradient, floating transparent header buttons, followed by the mobile app information row, stats, and full-width download CTA.
- **Desktop & Tablet Viewport (`>= md`)**:
  1. **Dedicated Desktop Navigation Bar**:
     - Sticky top bar with Back button (`← Back`), store breadcrumb (`Store › {Category} › {App Name}`), and quick action controls (Wishlist, Share, More options).
  2. **Side-by-Side 2-Column Hero (`grid-cols-12`)**:
     - **Left Column (7 cols)**: Large app squircle icon (120px+), publisher link, prominent app title, platform format and commercial badges, horizontal stats strip (Star rating, review count, content rating, downloads count, unified file size), and primary Download/Install button.
     - **Right Column (5 cols)**: Constrained, pristine 16:9 Banner & Video Trailer card (~420-480px wide by 236-270px tall) with rounded corners, subtle ambient border, dark mode ambient tint, and interactive YouTube trailer player with theater-mode and close controls.
  3. **Zero Vertical Bloat**:
     - App identity, call-to-action buttons, ratings, and media trailer all comfortably fit **above the fold** in desktop view, completely eliminating the mobile-centric stretched appearance.

